uter will sometimes have to rely  on something you came to imagination to  fill in the gaps  for example due to occlusion where parts  of the scene may be hidden from view one  of the most interesting characteristics  of our model is that we can effectively  fly through the computer's minds we can  ask it to smoothly move the camera in a  new scene and visually inspect how well  it can predict what that scene looks  like from different viewpoints this work  takes us one step closer towards  computers that learn to understand  scenes the way we do and crucially it  does this without any explicit human  supervision  you

